      "answer": "Self‑RAG learns to decide whether to retrieve during generation by having the language model predict a \"Retrieve\" token (yes/no/continue) based on the input and the partial output so far.  It then uses additional reflection tokens (ISREL, ISSUP, ISUSE) to judge relevance, support, and usefulness of the retrieved passage, allowing it to retrieve only when the passage is judged helpful.  In contrast, standard RAG simply retrieves the top‑scoring passage(s) before generation and does not condition retrieval on the generation context or perform fine‑grained relevance checks.",
